# SPECTRA - .dockerignore
#
# Status: session one. This file is the thing being delivered.
#
# Purpose: keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host state
# out of it. Part II section 74.0 allows exactly two network postures and the
# image build is on the NETWORK-FORBIDDEN side for everything except
# `make toolchain-refresh`. A host-resolved dependency cache, a host .venv or a
# host target/ directory copied into a context is how a resolver result leaks
# into an image that is supposed to be offline-complete.
#
# Rule: exclude broadly, then re-include the few paths a build stage actually
# needs. A path that must be inside an image belongs in a vendored bundle under
# /opt/spectra/vendor/<ecosystem>/ (Part II section 74.1.2), not in this context.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and repository metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.git/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.opencode

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host toolchain state - never copied into an image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.tox
**/.nox
**/.hypothesis
**/*.egg-info

# Rust
**/target
**/.cargo/registry
**/.cargo/git

# Go
**/go.work.sum.tmp

# Node / TypeScript
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.npm
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# .NET
**/bin
**/obj
**/.vs

# JVM
**/.gradle
**/build
**/.kotlin
**/.bloop
**/.metals
**/.bsp

# Haskell
**/dist-newstyle
**/.stack-work

# Native / CMake
**/CMakeFiles
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/cmake-build-*
**/compile_commands.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated and run-scoped data (Part I section 32.9)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/generated
data/runs
bench/results
out
bin
artifacts

# Toolchain OCI tarballs. Large, and already addressed by digest in images.lock.
cas/oci
cas/tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/credentials.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS and local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and prose: not needed to build an image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs
**/*.md
!README.md
# README.md is re-included because a stage may embed the project description.
# TODO(decision): if no stage ends up needing it, drop the re-include rather
# than leaving an unused file in the context.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Committed test data: excluded from image builds on purpose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/fixtures and data/golden are TRACKED in git and are mounted into a test
# run, not baked into a toolchain image. A fixture inside an image is a fixture
# nobody can see change.
data/fixtures
data/golden
tests/golden
